# Example Caddy config for prodbox. Caddy is the only thing facing the internet: the
# container port is bound to 127.0.0.1, and Caddy runs on the host (not inside
# docker/deploy/compose.deploy.yml), terminating TLS and reverse-proxying to the
# loopback port this stack's container published.
#
# Copy into /etc/caddy/Caddyfile alongside the pitchbox repo's own Caddy config and
# reload Caddy. The host and port below are already this stack's real values,
# nothing to replace.
#
# pitchbox.app (the apex) and www.pitchbox.app are this landing's real hosts as of
# #422: the apex used to point at the pitchbox app's own blue-green stack and now
# proxies here instead, with www 308-redirecting to it.
#
# app.pitchbox.app is a different stack - the dashboard, configured in the pitchbox
# repo, not this one. Do not add, remove, or touch its block from here.
#
# The DNS records must be grey-clouded (Cloudflare: DNS-only, proxy switch off)
# rather than orange-clouded, or Caddy cannot complete its own ACME challenge and
# terminate TLS directly:
#
#   pitchbox.app       A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; grey-clouded
#   www.pitchbox.app   A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; grey-clouded, redirects to the apex
#
# 127.0.0.1:5284 is reserved for a second stack under this repo (not yet built - see
# docker/deploy/secrets.env.example); when it exists it gets its own host block here,
# its own subdomain, and its own grey-clouded DNS record, the same shape as this one.

pitchbox.app {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5184
}

www.pitchbox.app {
	redir https://pitchbox.app{uri} 308
}
